To get the GNSS timestamp on Android, follow these steps:

1. First, ensure that you have the necessary permissions to access the location services. This can be done by adding the following lines of code in your AndroidManifest.xml file:

```xml
<uses-feature android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" />
```

2. Next, you need to request these permissions in your code using the ActivityCompat:

```java
ActivityCompat.requestPermissions(this, new String[]{android.Manifest.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION}, REQUEST_CODE);
```

3. Now that you have the permissions, you can use the LocationManager to request the GNSS information:

```java
LocationManager locationManager = (LocationManager) getSystemService(LOCATION_SERVICE);
String provider = LocationManager.GPS_PROVIDER;
String[] mLocationData = locationManager.getAllProviders();
```

4. Finally, you can get the GNSS timestamp from the mLocationData:

```java
for (String provider : mLocationData) {
    Location location = locationManager.getLastKnownLocation(provider);
    if (location instanceof GpsExcelProvider) {
        GpsExcelProvider locationProvider = (GpsExcelProvider) location;
        long timestamp = locationProvider.getTimeStampNS();
        System.out.println("GNSS timestamp: "+timestamp);
    }
}
```

This will give you the GNSS timestamp of your location provider.

